avformat/webvttdec: add an option to apply the X-TIMESTAMP-MAP header

Backport of FFmpeg commit 039335d9bc by Kacper Michajłow, as committed
upstream; the tests it adds are left out.

HLS WebVTT segments carry an X-TIMESTAMP-MAP header that maps a cue time
to an MPEG-TS time of the other renditions (RFC 8216, 3.5). With
timestamp_map set, add the offset it gives to the cue timestamps, and use
the 90 kHz MPEG-TS time base for the stream so that the mapping stays
exact. Skip the header when it comes in a block of its own instead of
ending the parsing there.

diff --git a/doc/demuxers.texi b/doc/demuxers.texi
index f787426..d669f45 100644
--- a/doc/demuxers.texi
+++ b/doc/demuxers.texi
@@ -1187,4 +1187,22 @@ this is set to 0, which means that a sensible value is chosen based on the
 input format.
 @end table
 
+@section webvtt
+
+WebVTT subtitle demuxer.
+
+It accepts the following options:
+
+@table @option
+@item kind
+Set the kind of the track: @samp{subtitles} (default), @samp{captions},
+@samp{descriptions} or @samp{metadata}.
+
+@item timestamp_map
+Apply the @code{X-TIMESTAMP-MAP} header of HLS WebVTT segments to the cue
+timestamps, which moves them onto the MPEG-TS timeline of the other
+renditions, and use the 90 kHz MPEG-TS time base for the stream. Default
+value is false.
+@end table
+
 @c man end DEMUXERS
